WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.930
In sunlight, a leaf pulls
water molecules apart.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.480
The oxygen released is just waste.

3
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.250
What the leaf wants is the electrons.

4
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.660
Light knocks an electron out
of a chlorophyll molecule,

5
00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.440
and electrons from water fill the gap.

6
00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:20.100
So where do those electrons end up,
and what do they make on the way?

7
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.260
In this mission, you'll follow one
electron through two photosystems,

8
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.500
boosted twice by light.

9
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.700
Then you'll compare the acidity
inside and outside a thylakoid,

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.300
and work out how big the difference is.

11
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.820
Your mission: find out
where the electrons end up,

12
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.430
and what they make on the way.
